# Quote CTAs → WhatsApp

All "Get a Quote", "Request a Quote", "Request Quote", and "Get Started" buttons must link to WhatsApp, not `/contact`.

## Single source of truth

Use **`settings.contact.whatsappUrl`** from `getSiteSettings()` (or pass it as a prop from a page that already fetched settings).

Do **not** introduce a second exported URL constant. Defaults live in `defaultSiteConfig.contact.whatsappUrl` inside `cms-defaults.ts` only.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — page already has or can fetch settings (React cache dedupes with layout)
const settings = await getSiteSettings();
<CTAButton href={settings.contact.whatsappUrl}>Request a Quote</CTAButton>

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded path or duplicate constant
<CTAButton href="/contact">Request a Quote</CTAButton>
import { WHATSAPP_QUOTE_URL } from "@/lib/content/cms-defaults";
```

## CMS defaults

Hero and CTA band `primaryCta.href` in `cms-defaults.ts` should match `defaultSiteConfig.contact.whatsappUrl`. CMS-stored sections override defaults — do not leave `/contact` in CMS data for quote buttons.

## Components

- Use `CTAButton` for quote actions (handles external links with `target="_blank"`).
- Nav "Contact" may still point to `/contact` (info page, not a quote CTA).
- `/contact` is contact details only — no lead form.

## Admin

If adding site-settings fields, include `contact.whatsappUrl` so the link is editable without code changes. Page-copy primary CTA href fields should default to the WhatsApp URL, not `/contact`.
